  <body>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      <b>POMDP for the coffee robot</b>
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      Model built by Jessy Hoey and encoded in the SPUDD format:
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~jhoey/research/spudd/">https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~jhoey/research/spudd</a>.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      It is included with the source code of Pascal Poupart&#8217;s software 
      Symbolic Perseus:
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      <a href="http://www.cs.uwaterloo.ca/ ~ ppoupart/software.html">http://www.cs.uwaterloo.ca/~ppoupart/software.html</a>.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      A direct link for this example is <a href="http://www.cs.uwaterloo.ca/~ppoupart/software/symbolicPerseus/problems/coffee/coffee3po.txt">http://www.cs.uwaterloo.ca/~ppoupart/software/symbolicPerseus/problems/coffee/coffee3po.txt</a>.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      Encoded in ProbModelXML by F. J. D&#237;ez in April 2010.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      <b>References:</b>
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      J. Hoey, R. St-Aubin, A. Hu, C. Boutilier.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      SPUDD: Stochastic planning using decision diagrams.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      In <i>Proceedings of the 15th Conference on Uncertainty in Artificial 
      Intelligence (UAI&#8217;99)</i>, Morgan Kaufmann, San Francisco, CA, 
      pages 279&#8211;288.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      M. Arias, F. J. D&#237;ez, M. A. Palacios-Alonso, M. Yebra, J. Fern&#225;ndez.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      POMDPs in OpenMarkov and ProbModelXML
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      <i>Seventh Annual Workshop on Multiagent Sequential Decision-Making 
      Under Uncertainty</i> (MSDM-2012), Valencia, Spain, 2012.
    </p>
  </body>
</html>]]></Comment>
